# Problem Child (bouyonmusique.com, wave 14 parity, 2026-10-20)
# Sources used:
# - NTS, artist page for Problem Child (opened 2026-10-20): born Johnny Fontainne aka Vincy Bad Boy, originates from St. Vincent, raised in Brooklyn, NYC, Vincy Road March wins in 2007 and 2009, collaborations with Beenie Man, Bunji Garlin and Voicemail, notable tracks Real Badboy, High Whole Night and Stick On, track Love De Road played on NTS.
# - Buzz.tt, performer page Problem Child ID 161 (opened 2026-10-20): Johnny Fontainne aka Vincy Bad Boy, born in St. Vincent, migrated to Brooklyn, Party Animal winner of the Vincy Road March 2007, Mad House second Vincy Road March title in 2009, spotlight on NBC Radio and HOT 97.1, collaborations Beenie Man Party Party, Voicemail High Whole Night, Bunji Garlin, Fay-Ann Lyons We Ready, Stick On released late spring 2011 on OBanga Productions, Ah Tink Ah Drunk with Tallpree on the Mad Blood Riddim.
# - Ebuzztt (opened 2026-10-20): St. Vincent Crowns Problem Child Road March Champ, Never Bow sealed the 2017 Road March title; Problem Child is Winning article (2019 season), St. Vincent born songwriter and artist, wrote with and for Patrice Roberts including A Little Wine, and for Shal Marshall; Vincy Soca Champ article (2025), real name Shertz James, Fraid Horn and Pong Pong took first and second place at Vincy Mas 2025 after winning the year before.
# - Vincypowa News, SVG Road March 2026 (opened 2026-10-20, reporting Carnival Development Corporation results dated 8 July 2026): Shertz "Problem Child" James, Party Time first with 53 points, third straight title, Carnival Jumbie took it in 2024, in 2025 Fraid Horn scored 100 and Pong Pong 97 for first and second, he did not contest the Soca Monarch in 2026.
# - Searchlight via NewsMemory, Songwriting is Big Business (2020, search result 2026-10-20): Problem Child among the most prolific Vincentian songwriters, had written for Patrice Roberts, Shal Marshall, Blaxx and Machel Montano.
# - Shazam and YouTube, Fym by Ridge and Problem Child (opened 2026-10-20): released 30 January 2025, YouTube auto generated credit Provided to YouTube by TuneCore, ℗ 2025 Ridge and Problem Child, full lyrics published on Shazam.
# - Black Island Girl Multimedia, Dominica Music Awards 2025 finalists (search result 2026-10-20): Collaboration of the Year finalist, Mr Ridge and Problem Child, FYM.
# - Qobuz, Summer Of Carnivals Vol. 1 album page (opened 2026-10-20): Problem Child tracks Carnival Jumbie, Like Never Before and B.O.T.S. (Battle of the Sexes), writer Shertz James, producer DJ Avalanche; Shazam credits on Dunce, New World Order and Real Souljahs also list Shertz James as lyric writer for Problem Child.
# - Groove Africa and Dulaxi (search results 2026-10-20): Identity by Pahjo with G-Sinnz and Problem Child, released 30 August 2024, penned by Patrick Joseph and Shertz James.
# - DJ mix tracklists on Listen Notes and TopPodcast (opened 2026-10-20): the Vincy Heat 2025 mix and the Soca Passport and Bouyon Passport mixes list Problem Child and Ridge, FYM, in the same running order as his Vincy Mas 2025 tracks Fraid Horn, Pong Pong and Happy Carnival.
# Note on the identity question: no source found for a separate Dominican or bouyon artist named Problem Child. Every 2024 and 2025 listing of FYM places it inside the Vincy artist run of releases, and the Dominica Music Awards listing is explained by his Dominican collaborator Mr Ridge. This profile therefore treats the FYM credit as the Saint Vincent artist, and says so openly.
# Note on names: older biographies publish the birth name Johnny Fontainne, while Ebuzztt in 2025 and the songwriting credits publish the real and writer name Shertz James. Both forms are printed here with their sources, neither is hidden.

